2. WEIGHT BREAKDOWN & REINFORCED GEOMETRY (PROVEN INDUSTRIAL SPECIFICATION)
The platform is designed entirely around the "Body-on-Frame" automotive principle, where in our case the cabin-integrated superstructure is positioned directly on top of the supporting inflatable tubes and locked via a proprietary patented scheme.
•	Rigid Spatial Framework (Framework with Integrated Transom Assembly): ~80 kg. Constructed entirely from standard commercial metal elements. The platform utilizes a unique, patented spatial geometry that evenly distributes dynamic outboard torque and extreme vibrational loads from a 40 HP motor across multiple structural frame attachment points. This architecture has undergone 9 years of rigorous evolutionary technical modifications and precise localized reinforcement in peak stress zones (fully recorded in a dedicated engineering summary ledger). Frame deformation, twisting, and transom area failure are completely eliminated. Zero expensive custom metal castings or specialized deck welding are required.
•	Inflatable Tubes, Integrated Drop-In Cabin & Protective Ecosystem: ~18 kg. The inflatable tubes are fabricated from PVC fabric of selected density with a mathematically calculated number of separate safety chambers, or from engineered thermoplastic polymer materials for challenging operational conditions. The drop-in inner cabin is tailored from heavy-duty PVC fabric, forming a single continuous capsule that inserts inside the chassis and locks to the frame, sheltering the passengers. The canopy has passed 9 years of exploitation from "April to November" without loss of properties.
•	Modular Deck Flooring: Lightweight elements of cost-effective composite decking. The floor is segmented into tight, CNC-machined, interlocking modules with a maximum length of 1 meter each, bolted directly to the metal chassis via intermediate structural connections. This configuration successfully minimizes the total number of welded nodes within the structural framework.
Please Note: Although the vessel's architecture gives a visual impression of structural simplicity, the platform consists of over 300 digitized parts and contains proprietary, hidden structural improvements thoroughly validated across 9 years of full-scale live stress tests. Full chemical specifications of materials, exact dimensions of structural elements, localized reinforcement layout charts, specific deck component materials, technological maps, and manufacturers of the specialized protective textiles, internal spatial layout nodes, specific interior cabin pocket layout blueprints, as well as the comprehensive summary ledger of engineering updates over 9 years, constitute strict trade secrets. These data packages will be fully disclosed to the receiving party exclusively upon the execution of a standard Non-Disclosure and Non-Circumvention Agreement (NDA/NNN).
