3. LOGISTICAL EFFICIENCY & CKD FREIGHT METRICS
•	SUV Portability: The entire metal chassis and structural deck elements consist of compact segments no longer than 1 meter each. When disassembled, the 4.5-meter catamaran fits into a standard car trunk, without using a boat trailer.
•	Container Freight Optimization: Traditional rigid RIB boats allow a maximum of 2–4 assembled units per standard maritime shipping container. The "Aquamobile" detachable architecture allows for compact cargo consolidation. Complete units can be consolidated inside a single container as Completely Knocked Down (CKD) machine kits, allowing regional dealer networks to clear customs under low-tariff "spare parts and components" classifications.
•	Field Maintainability: The vessel's engineered configuration enables rapid field repairs directly at a boat slip or shoreline, facilitating immediate element-by-element replacement of any damaged segment based on standard automotive maintenance principles, entirely eliminating the need to transport the entire watercraft to a specialized service center.
•	Storage Modularity (Optional Equipment / Add-on): For ultimate operational versatility, an auxiliary device has been engineered—a specialized transport trailer on pivoting axles. This device is strictly optional (premium add-on) and enables a single operator to fully detach both inflatable tubes in under 30 minutes (for proper indoor winter storage), or, thanks to the utilization of our proprietary design, can be used for localized maintenance or servicing.
